<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<?import javafx.scene.control.ScrollPane?>
<?import javafx.scene.layout.VBox?>
<?import javafx.scene.text.Text?>
<?import javafx.scene.text.TextFlow?>
<?import javafx.scene.image.ImageView?>
<?import javafx.scene.layout.HBox?>
<?import javafx.scene.control.Label?>

<ScrollPane
        xmlns="http://javafx.com/javafx/21"
        xmlns:fx="http://javafx.com/fxml/1"
        fx:controller="com.example.game.gui.HowToPlayController"
        fitToWidth="true"
>


   <VBox spacing="10">
      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 24px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Game Manual</Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            Welcome to the built-in manual of game Light Bulbs. Here you can find all necessary
            information about the game, how to play and about some hidden features.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 18px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Basic Principles</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            The game is about rotating power source, light bulb and wire cells until all
            light bulbs are powered on. You can either load your save and continue or generate
            a new game. Difficulty can be modified by setting the size of game map, changing timer,
            amount of empty cells and shuffling strength.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 18px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Cell Types</Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <HBox spacing="10" alignment="CENTER_LEFT">
         <ImageView fx:id="powerSourceImage" fitHeight="50.0" fitWidth="50.0" />
         <Label text="power source" />
      </HBox>

      <HBox spacing="10" alignment="CENTER_LEFT">
         <ImageView fx:id="lightBulbImage" fitHeight="50.0" fitWidth="50.0" />
         <Label text="light bulb" />
      </HBox>

      <HBox spacing="10" alignment="CENTER_LEFT">
         <ImageView fx:id="wireImage" fitHeight="50.0" fitWidth="50.0" />
         <Label text="wire connector" />
      </HBox>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            These cells come in different configurations which denote connectable sides and whether
            they are powered on or off.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 16px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Basic Controls</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            The game is controlled by clicking on the game cells, which rotates them. Empty cells
            can not be rotated. When all light bulbs are lit up, the game is won. You lose the game
            when the timer timeouts. After the game is finished, the game cells become inactive to your
            clicks.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 18px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Help View</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            Help View can be opened by clicking on the Help View button in the top menu. It opens
            a new window which shows how many rotations are needed on each cell so that the game is won.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 18px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Undo and Redo</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            If you wish to go back then you can. You can use the Undo button in the top menu. But beware
            that going back will not decrease your turn count. Redo is also supported and behaves how you would
            expect.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 18px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Auto Solving</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            If you feel tired, then you can use the built-in auto solver, which will lock the game
            and solve the game step by step. Once turned on, it cannot be disabled
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>

      <TextFlow>
         <Text style="-fx-font-size: 18px; -fx-font-weight: bold;">Gameplay Tips</Text>
      </TextFlow>
      <TextFlow>
         <Text>
            Hovering over a cell shows tooltip with the count of total rotations so far. If you
            do that after the game finishes information about the remaining amount of turns is
            also displayed.
         </Text>
      </TextFlow>
   </VBox>
</ScrollPane>
